1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,230
Sales enablement without an AI layer is

2
00:00:02,280 --> 00:00:04,240
becoming a content management problem

3
00:00:04,330 --> 00:00:05,900
instead of a performance problem.

4
00:00:06,620 --> 00:00:08,660
Most enablement teams spend the majority

5
00:00:08,710 --> 00:00:10,430
of their time creating and organizing

6
00:00:10,480 --> 00:00:10,960
content.

7
00:00:11,590 --> 00:00:14,060
Playbooks, battle cards, objection

8
00:00:14,120 --> 00:00:15,920
guides, onboarding materials.

9
00:00:16,540 --> 00:00:18,010
The content exists.

10
00:00:18,370 --> 00:00:20,600
The problem is that reps cannot find it

11
00:00:20,630 --> 00:00:22,640
when they need it, and when they do find

12
00:00:22,700 --> 00:00:24,150
it, it is often out of date.

13
00:00:24,690 --> 00:00:26,450
AI changes the enablement model.

14
00:00:26,900 --> 00:00:28,670
It can surface the right content at the

15
00:00:28,740 --> 00:00:30,480
right moment based on the context of the

16
00:00:30,510 --> 00:00:30,780
deal.

17
00:00:31,400 --> 00:00:32,740
It can identify which reps are

18
00:00:32,770 --> 00:00:34,360
struggling with specific objections

19
00:00:34,430 --> 00:00:36,340
based on call data and serve them

20
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:37,230
targeted coaching.

21
00:00:37,640 --> 00:00:39,880
It can analyze win and loss patterns and

22
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:41,800
update the playbook automatically when

23
00:00:41,830 --> 00:00:42,670
the market shifts.

24
00:00:43,160 --> 00:00:45,000
Enablement stops being a library and

25
00:00:45,050 --> 00:00:46,730
starts being a real-time performance

26
00:00:46,750 --> 00:00:47,100
system.

27
00:00:47,880 --> 00:00:49,820
The teams that make this shift stop

28
00:00:49,940 --> 00:00:52,310
measuring enablement by content volume

29
00:00:52,430 --> 00:00:54,140
and start measuring it by rep

30
00:00:54,230 --> 00:00:55,180
performance improvement.

31
00:00:55,900 --> 00:00:57,320
That is the metric that matters.

32
00:00:57,460 --> 00:01:00,050
Follow A-Gent for the agent-first GTM

33
00:01:00,090 --> 00:01:00,510
playbook.
